       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 10 mg once daily. Doses that high risk severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Amlodipine's half-life is long, so the effects can last a long time. Your patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change this.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **5 mg** by mouth once daily, the usual starting dose.\n- **10 mg** by mouth once daily, the maximum dose.\n- **2.5 mg** by mouth once daily, a lower starting dose sometimes used in frail patients or those on other antihypertensives.\n\nIf 50 mg is what you intend, tell me and include the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with a note, though pharmacy will probably want to verify it. If you give me the correct dose, I'll enter it right away."
      }
